      "level": 2,
      "content": "FORCE AND LAWS OF MOTION"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Force causes changes in an object's state of motion, velocity, or direction.",
        "Inertia is the inherent property of a body to resist any change in its state of rest or uniform motion.",
        "Linear momentum is the product of mass and velocity, conserved in isolated systems.",
        "Friction opposes relative motion between contacting surfaces and varies across static, kinetic, and rolling types.",
        "Weight varies with gravitational acceleration, whereas mass remains constant regardless of location."
      ],
      "id": "59bzrud"
    },
